    issue('tuning-domain-and-data-dependence',[13],'The numerator -2log(alpha)+log(-2log(alpha))+1 in rho_m can be negative for alpha sufficiently close to1, while the source generally allows alpha∈(0,1). A further domain restriction would be required for that displayed square root to be real. Rho_m also depends on estimated variance at the first peeking time, so it must not be replaced by arbitrary fixed rho in the sharp-coverage theorem.')
