    issue('uncentered-and-misspecified-influence',[17,18,19,22],'Formula24 is explicitly an uncentered EIF; subtracting psi would change the AIPW estimator25. Formula27 uses potentially misspecified regression limits with the true propensity. T3.1 allows such limits, whereas T3.2 requires consistent nuisance functions and convergence to the efficient f. Its common-setup reference does not reimpose known propensity.')
    issue('fold-size-and-variance-conventions',[16,17],'The infinity-subscript split streams are counted at current time t by an explicit convention. Early times may leave a fold empty; the source does not define all estimator/variance values then. Variance26 averages two fold variances equally, not by random fold size, and the within-fold normalization is named sample variance rather than reprinted. Preserve these choices and ambiguities.')
